sub:assertion {
<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/levin-2023-glue-08> a <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/Claim>;
    dc:description "In deer trophic memory, an ectopic branch is formed in the otherwise stereotyped antler at the location of earlier damage year after year, long after the damaged rack has been shed, a memory of 3D position held by scalp cells that regenerate the antler annually.";
    dc:type "empirical-generalization";
    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Deer antlers re-form an ectopic branch at a past injury site year after year";
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/context> "Levin M, “Bioelectric networks: the cognitive glue enabling evolutionary scaling from physiology to mind”, Animal cognition (2023), doi:10.1007/s10071-023-01780-3; section “Basal cognition without neurons: what dynamic bodies think about › Memory and target morphology”. Scope: Deer (Cervidae) antler regeneration"
}
